@@ -8,6 +8,41 @@ This guide connects a new LLM provider to Harness.
 
 An LLM adapter extends `LlmAdapter` and implements `stream()`, translating Harness's provider-neutral request into a provider API call and translating the response back into Harness chunks.
 
+## Understand the design first
+
+`LlmAdapter` translates one model call. It does not manage sessions, decide when to call a model, or execute tools.
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+  A["Agent loop"] --> B["LlmRuntime"]
+  B --> C["LlmAdapter"]
+  C --> D["Provider API"]
+  D --> C
+  C --> B
+  B --> A
+```
+
+| Component | Responsibility |
+|---|---|
+| Agent loop | Decides when to request a model and handles tool calls returned by the model |
+| `LlmRuntime` | Selects an adapter by `provider` and validates model capabilities and request configuration |
+| `LlmAdapter` | Converts requests, calls the provider API, and emits the shared response chunks |
+| Provider API | Performs the actual model inference |
+
+One request follows these steps:
+
+1. `LlmAdapter` receives `GenerateOptions`.
+2. The adapter converts messages, tools, and generation parameters into the provider request format.
+3. The adapter starts one streaming API request.
+4. The adapter converts provider data into `StreamChunk` values.
+5. The adapter ends the call with `finish`.
+
+Keep three boundaries in mind:
+
+- One `stream()` call represents one provider attempt; policy at the agent-step boundary handles retries.
+- Model-visible history comes from the session log; the adapter does not keep its own conversation copy.
+- Provider-specific fields stay inside the adapter; its public interface uses only Harness types.
+
